  "steps": [
    {
      "step_id": "tile_pandas_descriptive_stats.s01",
      "type": "explainer",
      "concept_ids": [
        "stats.pandas_descriptive_stats"
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Descriptive Statistics",
      "title": "Computing statistics directly from a column",
      "lede": "pandas can compute the mean, median, and standard deviation you've calculated by hand — straight from a DataFrame column.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_pandas_descriptive_stats.s01.b1",
          "role": "intro",
          "text": "The mean, median, and standard deviation computed by hand earlier for the seven-value delivery-time batch are exactly what pandas can compute directly from a DataFrame column.",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "stats.pandas_descriptive_stats"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "stats.pandas_descriptive_stats#tb1"
            ],
            "fact_ids": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_pandas_descriptive_stats.s01.b2",
          "role": "definition",
          "text": "pandas provides built-in statistical methods for a Series or DataFrame column, including `mean()` (mean of values), `median()` (arithmetic median), and `std()` (sample standard deviation): if `delivery_time_minutes` holds all fourteen orders, `orders[\"delivery_time_minutes\"].mean()`, `.median()`, and `.std()` return approximately 29.0, 25.0, and 15.6 minutes.",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "stats.pandas_descriptive_stats"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "stats.pandas_descriptive_stats#tb2"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "stats.pandas_descriptive_stats#f1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_pandas_descriptive_stats.s01.b3",
          "role": "definition",
          "text": "`describe()` computes a set of summary statistics — count, mean, std, min, quartiles, and max — for a Series or for each numeric column of a DataFrame in one call: `orders[\"delivery_time_minutes\"].describe()` returns all of those figures at once for the delivery-time column.",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "stats.pandas_descriptive_stats"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "stats.pandas_descriptive_stats#tb3"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "stats.pandas_descriptive_stats#f2"
            ]
          }
        },
